manufact               package:AA                    R Documentation

Data on Faults in a Manufacturing Process

Description:

     The 'manufact' data frame has 22 rows and 3 columns.

     Data on faults in a manufacturing process.  Each of 22 batches of
     raw  material was divided into two parts and processed by one of
     two  methods ('standard' and 'modified').  The response is the
     presence or  absence of faults in the finished product.  A single
     covariate, purity  index, was measured before the processing.

Usage:

     data(manufact)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'standard' the number of faults in a manufacturing process using
          the standard method;

     'modified' the number of faults in a manufacturing process using
          the modified method;

     'purity' the purity index measured before the processing.

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Cox, D.R. and Snell, E.J.(1981).  _Applied Statistics: Principles
     and Examples_.  Chapman & Hall, London.  Example H.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Problem 28.
